#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A scripted stand-in for Claude Code, pi and Codex, so the demo needs no account,
costs nothing and plays the same every time. Run as claude, pi or codex (bin/, on the
demo's PATH, which tells it which in FAKE_AGENT), roster starts it as that agent, and it reports as
that agent does: Claude through the hooks roster gives it (`--settings`), pi as
roster's extension would, Codex as its hooks would (both through `roster report`).
It keeps the agent's own kind of transcript, answers roster's questions as the agent
would (its account's limits, a one-off title), and sets the pane title as Claude
does. What it does after a prompt comes from SCENARIOS, by keyword; every name,
path and figure in it is made up."""

